# The rulebook's ousting example (vekn.net/rulebook, "Ending the Game"): Justine, Lisa, Richard,
# Scott and Steve sit clockwise in that order. Whoever ousts them, a Methuselah gains 1 VP and 6
# pool when their prey is ousted, and the next Methuselah on becomes their prey. The last one left
# gains 1 more VP. The most VP wins, ousted or not.
seed 5
seat J justine
seat L lisa
seat R richard
seat S scott
seat T steve
crypt J "Vera Nightfall" *12
library J "Iron Ward" *40
crypt L "Tomas Grey" *12
library L "Quick Feed" *40
crypt R "Ilse Várga" *12
library R "Gate Hound" *40
crypt S "Vera Nightfall" *12
library S "Iron Ward" *40
crypt T "Tomas Grey" *12
library T "Quick Feed" *40
start

# Steve is ousted first: he is Scott's prey, so Scott gains 6 pool and 1 VP.
J> pool -30 T
expect ousted T true
expect vp S 1
expect pool S 36
log public T was ousted; S gains 1 VP and 6 pool

# Scott is ousted next, by Richard: Scott is Richard's prey, so Richard gains 6 pool and 1 VP. Scott
# keeps his VP.
R> pool -36 S
expect vp R 1
expect pool R 36
expect vp S 1

# Lisa is ousted next, so Justine gains 6 pool and 1 VP.
J> pool -30 L
expect vp J 1
expect pool J 36

# Justine and Richard are each other's prey. Richard's pool doesn't save him: Justine gains 1 VP
# for her prey, and 1 more for being the last Methuselah left.
J> pool -36 R
expect vp J 3
expect vp R 1
expect vp S 1
expect vp L 0
expect vp T 0
expect ended last-standing
expect winner J
expect gamewin J
